:: EncyclopediaDeath [encyclopedia]
<<nobr>>
    Hi hello, placeholder page as this is currently a minor bit of lore.<br><br>

    Dragons—or at least the colony <<print $player.title>> was raised in—believe the dead need to return to Sun and Moon above in order to escape the world of the living.<br><br>

    However, the dead have no fire with which to warm their wings and guide them higher. Thus, the living do two things:<br><br>

    First, a cairn is constructed. This is a launching point for the dead; a high point, built upon the bones of the colony's fallen, where they may attempt to throw themselves to the sky and stars.<br><br>

    Second, a stone tablet is erected. Dragons offer fire to this tablet, warming it as best they can. The dead claim this fire for themselves, cooling the tablet, and use this gifted inner-fire to guide their rise to Sun and Moon.<br><br>

    They might still fail and fall to the world. If this is the case, and no more is offered, fireless dragons will attempt to steal warmth and fire from the hearts of living dragons to attempt their ascension again. If a dragon dies of this leeching, they are only more bones to raise the cairn higher.
<</nobr>>